1
00:00:03,217 --> 00:00:08,217
In 1994, Peter Shor showed that a quantum computer could factor huge numbers,

2
00:00:08,217 --> 00:00:11,294
and break the encryption that protects the internet.

3
00:00:11,294 --> 00:00:16,294
Thirty years later, no quantum computer has done it at a useful scale.

4
00:00:16,294 --> 00:00:17,832
The reason is noise.

5
00:00:18,517 --> 00:00:20,055
We are Team PhASE,

6
00:00:20,055 --> 00:00:25,440
and Below Threshold is an interactive playground that takes you from a single qubit,

7
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:29,671
through Shor's algorithm, to the error correction that keeps it alive.
